      <h1>US Battery Manufacturers</h1>
      <p class="muted">Manufacturer Directory · Last reviewed 2026-09-17</p>

      <div class="box">
        <strong>Direct answer:</strong> US battery manufacturing runs in two layers: a
        <strong>lead-acid incumbent layer</strong> — <strong>Clarios</strong> (the world's largest automotive
        battery maker, Milwaukee-headquartered) and <strong>EnerSys</strong> (industrial motive and reserve
        power) — and an <strong>IRA-driven lithium layer</strong> of cell plants from <strong>Tesla</strong>,
        <strong>LG Energy Solution</strong>, <strong>SK On</strong>, <strong>Panasonic</strong> and others,
        pulled onto US soil by production credits and automaker demand.
      </div>

